# OpenField configuration. Copy to .env and edit — every line is optional.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# With no .env at all, OpenField talks to ComfyUI on 127.0.0.1:8188 and writes
# renders to ~/openfield-output. That is enough to run.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- engine ----

# Where ComfyUI is answering.
# COMFY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8188

# Every job runs through the Comfy SDK against Comfy API v2. Locally that is
# comfy-api-proxy in front of ComfyUI (pip install comfy-api-proxy); OpenField
# starts it for you if it is on PATH or named here.
# COMFY_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8189
# COMFY_PROXY_BIN=comfy-api-proxy
#
# Run on Comfy Cloud instead (paid Comfy Cloud plan, all models must exist there):
# COMFY_BASE_URL=https://cloud.comfy.org
# COMFY_API_KEY=comfyui-...

# Command that starts ComfyUI, used by the START ENGINE button and by autostart.
# Add --preview-method auto (or start ComfyUI with it yourself) to get live
# step-by-step previews while a shot renders.
# Leave unset and OpenField never tries to launch anything — it just reports the
# engine as down and you start it yourself.
#
#   Linux / macOS:
# COMFY_LAUNCH=/home/you/ComfyUI/venv/bin/python /home/you/ComfyUI/main.py --preview-method auto
#   WSL driving a Windows install:
# COMFY_LAUNCH=cmd.exe /c start "" C:\path\to\ComfyUI\run.bat --preview-method auto

# Seconds to wait for the engine to answer after launching it.
# COMFY_LAUNCH_TIMEOUT=120

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- models ----

# ComfyUI's models/ folder — the one holding diffusion_models/, vae/, loras/.
# Only `npm run models` uses this; the app asks the running engine instead.
# COMFY_MODELS_DIR=/home/you/ComfyUI/models

# Needed for gated repos (LTX-2.x). Accept the licence on the HuggingFace model
# page first, then paste a read token here.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# A folder of loose .safetensors mapped into ComfyUI via extra_model_paths.
# OpenField reads each file's header to tell a LoRA from a full model, so each one
# is only offered where it can actually work. Unset = feature is inert.
# SPICE_DIR=/path/to/extra/ltx/models

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- local ----

# Video render size when Setup has no choice: 480p, 720p or 1080p. Unset = from
# the GPU: 24 GB or more renders at 720p, smaller cards at 480p. A choice made
# in Setup > Render size still wins.
# OPENFIELD_RENDER_TIER=720p

# Where renders go when no project is selected.
# OPENFIELD_OUTPUT=/home/you/openfield-output

# Port, and the interface to bind. OpenField HAS NO AUTHENTICATION — only move it
# off loopback on a network you trust.
# OPENFIELD_PORT=3161
# OPENFIELD_HOST=127.0.0.1
# UI port for `npm run dev` (Vite). `npm start` serves the UI on OPENFIELD_PORT.
# OPENFIELD_UI_PORT=3160

# "Film it on your phone" (Mirror, Reshoot). While the QR code is showing, and
# only then, a separate listener answers on the LAN on this port: one mobile page
# and one upload, behind a single-use token, closing after 10 minutes or the first
# clip. The main server above never leaves loopback.
# OPENFIELD_PHONE_PORT=3162
# LAN address to bind and put in the QR code, if auto-detection picks the wrong
# one. Under WSL2 NAT networking, set it to Windows' LAN address (the UI shows the
# netsh portproxy command; networkingMode=mirrored in .wslconfig avoids all this).
# OPENFIELD_PHONE_HOST=192.168.1.20

# Optional: transcribe generated dialogue onto each video take.
# WHISPER_BIN=/home/you/miniconda3/bin/whisper
# FFMPEG_BIN=ffmpeg
# ffprobe, if it is not next to FFMPEG_BIN.
# FFPROBE_BIN=ffprobe

# Optional: an OpenAI-compatible server (llama.cpp, LM Studio, vLLM, ...) the Scene planner asks after the engine
# and before Ollama. URL is the base up to and including /v1. Without MODEL the first one from /v1/models is used;
# KEY is sent as a Bearer token when set.
# OPENFIELD_LLM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1
# OPENFIELD_LLM_MODEL=
# OPENFIELD_LLM_KEY=

# Optional: a local Ollama the Scene planner falls back to. MODEL is a comma list; the first one installed is used.
# OPENFIELD_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# OPENFIELD_OLLAMA_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b,qwen3:30b,qwen3:8b,gemma3:12b

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- judge ----

# Judge preview (docs/RUNPOD.md): a password on every route, draft limits and a
# daily render cap, for a rented GPU that is up only while people look at it.
# Binds 0.0.0.0 unless OPENFIELD_HOST says otherwise. The server refuses to start
# with judge mode on and no password (8 characters or more).
# OPENFIELD_JUDGE=1
# OPENFIELD_JUDGE_PASSWORD=
# Renders per UTC day across all apps (default 20).
# OPENFIELD_JUDGE_CAP=20

# Where job history, the input cache and the proxy's job state live (default data/).
# OPENFIELD_DATA=/workspace/openfield-data

